{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And when you slaughter, etc.</b> This passage was stated only to teach that their slaughter must be on condition to eat within this time — for if to fix them a time of eating, it has already been stated (Leviticus 7): ״וְאִם נֶדֶר אוֹ נְדָבָה זֶבַח קָרְבָּנוֹ״ etc. (Sifra)." "<b>For your acceptance you shall slaughter it.</b> The beginning of its slaughter must be on condition of satisfaction — that it be for you an acceptance; for if you contemplate upon it a disqualifying thought, it is not accepted on your behalf before Me." "<b>לרצנכם.</b> אפיי״צימנטו — this is according to its plain sense; and our Sages learned from here for one who engages in consecrated offerings that are disqualified, that he must intend to slaughter (Zevachim 47; Chullin 13)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "the la'az אפיי״צימנטו is Old French à pescimen (à peschenin), 'for fish-bait,' Rashi's plain-sense rendering of לרצנכם here understood as 'for your trapping/baiting.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:05.727761594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}